flowchart TB
  accTitle: Offline VM architecture and acceptance boundaries
  accDescr: A terminal controls an isolated QEMU KVM guest over a host UNIX serial socket. Optional management VNC is host loopback only. The guest has no network interface or normal guest network path. Workbench and REA are separate, with their integration not implemented. Scope A is conditionally accepted; scope B is not accepted and original A4 failure is retained.

  operator[Operator terminal] --> serial[Host UNIX serial socket]
  vnc[Optional VNC management\nHost loopback only] -.-> vm
  iso[Read-only offline ISO\nMounted noexec / nosuid / nodev] --> vm
  serial --> vm

  subgraph vm[Isolated QEMU / KVM guest]
    direction TB
    resources[2 vCPU · 4 GiB RAM · 20 GiB qcow2]
    network[No guest NIC\nNo normal guest network path]
    node[Node 22.23.3] --> workbench[Workbench MCP\nBasic SQLite + doctor\n16-tool-list smoke passed]
    scanner[Real scanner operation not verified]
    rea[REA 6.7.0] --> analysis[JDK 21.0.12.1 + Ghidra 12.1.4\nDiagnostic / analysis path]
    workbench -.- future[REA / Workbench integration\nNOT implemented · separate TASK113]
    future -.- rea
  end

  subgraph acceptance[Acceptance boundary]
    direction LR
    scopeA[Scope A: VM base / basic operation\nCONDITIONALLY ACCEPTED]
    scopeB[Scope B: analysis\nNOT ACCEPTED\nOriginal A4 FAIL retained]
    disclaimer[No production-safety claim]
  end

  classDef accepted fill:#e8f4ed,stroke:#43825a,color:#153d25
  classDef warning fill:#fff0dc,stroke:#b7791f,color:#633d0b
  classDef rejected fill:#fce8e6,stroke:#b94a48,color:#701e1c
  classDef muted fill:#f1f3f5,stroke:#7b8794,color:#344054
  class scopeA accepted
  class scopeB rejected
  class future warning
  class network,scanner,disclaimer muted
